Extend a Stage-2 win into a full TXOP for P-EDCA
=================================================

Applies ON TOP OF the already-applied pedca_patch.patch (i.e. against your
current, already-patched ns-3.48 tree), not against vanilla ns-3.

Problem being fixed
--------------------
Currently, ExitPedcaStage2() is called unconditionally, right at the top of
QosFrameExchangeManager::TransmissionSucceeded(), as soon as the Stage-2
winner's first RTS/CTS + data + ack exchange concludes -- see the "Step 6
exit path" comment there. That means a Stage-2 win only ever buys the
station ONE protected frame: even if AC_VO's TxopLimit and remaining TXOP
time would allow more frames to go out back-to-back under the SAME channel
hold (ordinary EDCA TXOP bursting, governed by the unmodified
`if (m_edca->GetTxopLimit(...).IsStrictlyPositive() && ...)` block right
below the P-EDCA insertion), the very next line already zeroed out the
Stage-2 state before that check even runs.

Fix
---
1. Only call ExitPedcaStage2() when the TXOP is actually ending (reusing
   the exact TxopLimit/RemainingTxop condition the unmodified code already
   uses to decide TXOP continuation) -- not unconditionally after the
   first frame.
2. Because GetPsduProtection() currently forces RTS/CTS for EVERY frame
   sent while IsPedcaStage2() is true, simply keeping Stage 2 "open" for
   the rest of the TXOP would force RTS/CTS before every continuation
   frame too -- wasteful and non-standard (a TXOP's later frames are
   already protected by the NAV the first frame's own Duration field set,
   exactly like ordinary EDCA TXOP bursting for every other AC). So this
   patch adds a one-shot "initial frame" flag, consumed the first time
   GetPsduProtection() forces RTS for a given Stage-2 win, so only that
   first frame is forced through RTS/CTS -- subsequent frames in the same
   TXOP fall through to ordinary (usually no-RTS) protection decisions.

Net effect: a Stage-2 win now reserves the medium (and keeps legacy/
ineligible STAs deferred via the DS-CTS's NAV) for the station's whole
TXOP, not just its first frame, while still only spending one RTS/CTS
exchange to establish that reservation -- matching ordinary 802.11 TXOP
semantics for the frames after the first.

--- a/src/wifi/model/qos-txop.h
+++ b/src/wifi/model/qos-txop.h
@@ -397,6 +397,16 @@ class QosTxop : public Txop
      * @return true if this AC is currently in the P-EDCA Stage-2 restricted-contention window
      *         on the given link
      */
     bool IsPedcaStage2(uint8_t linkId) const;
+    /**
+     * Query-and-consume the "initial frame of this Stage-2 win still pending RTS/CTS
+     * protection" flag for the given link. Returns true (and clears the flag) the first time
+     * this is called after EnterPedcaStage2() -- i.e. for the TXOP's first, RTS/CTS-protected
+     * frame -- and false on every subsequent call until the next EnterPedcaStage2(), i.e. for
+     * any further frames sent within the same Stage-2-won TXOP. Not const: this call has the
+     * side effect of consuming the flag, matching how PSRC/QSRC increments elsewhere in this
+     * class are one-shot per real transmission attempt.
+     * @param linkId the ID of the given link
+     * @return true if this is the Stage-2 win's initial (RTS/CTS-forced) frame
+     */
+    bool ConsumePedcaStage2InitialFrame(uint8_t linkId);
     /**
      * @return the ANA-assigned RA used to identify a DS-CTS frame
      */
@@ -469,6 +479,10 @@ class QosTxop : public Txop
         };
 
         PedcaPhase pedcaPhase{PedcaPhase::NORMAL}; //!< current P-EDCA phase
         EventId pedcaStage2Timeout;                //!< Stage-2 window expiry event
+        bool pedcaStage2InitialFramePending{false}; //!< true until the Stage-2 win's first
+                                                     //!< (RTS/CTS-forced) frame has been sent;
+                                                     //!< see ConsumePedcaStage2InitialFrame()
     };

--- a/src/wifi/model/qos-txop.cc
+++ b/src/wifi/model/qos-txop.cc
@@ -393,6 +393,7 @@ void
 QosTxop::EnterPedcaStage2(uint8_t linkId, Time window)
 {
     NS_LOG_FUNCTION(this << +linkId << window.As(Time::US));
     auto& link = GetLink(linkId);
     link.pedcaPhase = QosLinkEntity::PedcaPhase::STAGE2;
+    link.pedcaStage2InitialFramePending = true;
     link.cw = GetMinCw(linkId); // now resolves to m_pedcaStage2CwMin
     GenerateBackoff(linkId);
     RequestAccess(linkId);
@@ -424,6 +425,7 @@ QosTxop::ExitPedcaStage2(uint8_t linkId)
     {
         return; // already left through another exit path; nothing to do
     }
     NS_LOG_FUNCTION(this << +linkId);
+    link.pedcaStage2InitialFramePending = false;
     if (link.pedcaStage2Timeout.IsPending())
     {
         link.pedcaStage2Timeout.Cancel();
     }
     link.pedcaPhase = QosLinkEntity::PedcaPhase::NORMAL;
     link.cw = GetMinCw(linkId);
     GenerateBackoff(linkId);
     // Other ACs' backoff resumption times, pushed forward by DisableEdcaFor above, are not
     // un-pushed here: there is no API to cancel that early, so on an early exit (e.g. we won
     // Stage 2 well before the window would have timed out) other ACs stay paused a little
     // longer than strictly necessary. If PedcaEligible(linkId) is still true, the very next
     // NotifyAccessRequested() call re-enters DS_CTS_PENDING immediately.
 }
+
+bool
+QosTxop::ConsumePedcaStage2InitialFrame(uint8_t linkId)
+{
+    auto& link = GetLink(linkId);
+    if (link.pedcaPhase != QosLinkEntity::PedcaPhase::STAGE2 ||
+        !link.pedcaStage2InitialFramePending)
+    {
+        return false;
+    }
+    link.pedcaStage2InitialFramePending = false;
+    return true;
+}

--- a/src/wifi/model/qos-frame-exchange-manager.cc
+++ b/src/wifi/model/qos-frame-exchange-manager.cc
@@ -682,14 +682,29 @@ QosFrameExchangeManager::TransmissionSucceeded()
         return;
     }

-    if (m_edca->IsPedcaStage2(m_linkId))
-    {
-        // Step 6 exit path: we won Stage 2, and the RTS/CTS + data + ack exchange it forced has
-        // now concluded successfully. Leave Stage 2; if more AC_VO frames remain and QSRC/PSRC
-        // still allow it, the next NotifyAccessRequested() re-enters DS_CTS_PENDING on its own.
-        m_edca->ExitPedcaStage2(m_linkId);
-    }
+    if (m_edca->IsPedcaStage2(m_linkId))
+    {
+        if (m_edca->GetTxopLimit(m_linkId).IsStrictlyPositive() &&
+            m_edca->GetRemainingTxop(m_linkId) > m_phy->GetSifs())
+        {
+            // TXOP continues under the same channel hold Stage 2 already won: stay in Stage 2
+            // so the exit (and P-EDCA bookkeeping) happens once the whole TXOP ends, not after
+            // its first frame. GetPsduProtection() only forces RTS/CTS for the TXOP's initial
+            // frame (QosTxop::ConsumePedcaStage2InitialFrame), so this and later continuation
+            // frames fall through to ordinary protection decisions, exactly like TXOP
+            // continuation frames for any other AC -- they're already covered by the NAV the
+            // first frame's own Duration field set.
+            NS_LOG_DEBUG("Won Stage 2, TXOP continues: staying in Stage 2 until TXOP ends");
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            // Step 6 exit path: we won Stage 2, and either this was a single-frame TXOP or
+            // there is no more TXOP time/no more frames left. Leave Stage 2; if more AC_VO
+            // frames remain and QSRC/PSRC still allow it, the next NotifyAccessRequested()
+            // re-enters DS_CTS_PENDING on its own.
+            m_edca->ExitPedcaStage2(m_linkId);
+        }
+    }

     if (m_edca->GetTxopLimit(m_linkId).IsStrictlyPositive() &&
         m_edca->GetRemainingTxop(m_linkId) > m_phy->GetSifs())
     {

(TransmissionFailed() is intentionally left unchanged: a failed RTS/CTS
means the reservation was never actually established for this attempt --
most likely a Stage-2 collision with another P-EDCA STA's RTS -- so exiting
Stage 2 immediately, rather than trying to continue a TXOP that was never
secured, is still correct.)

