Notes / things to verify before you rely on this for results
--------------------------------------------------------------
1. Line numbers/context above are anchored to the hunks I was shown from
   pedca_patch.patch, not a full compile of your tree -- match by the
   quoted surrounding lines/comments rather than assuming exact line
   numbers, and expect to nudge the hunks by hand if `patch`/`git apply`
   complains about offset.
2. This assumes QosTxop::GetTxopLimit()/GetRemainingTxop() are already
   available and behave as used by the unmodified continuation check right
   below the edit in TransmissionSucceeded() -- they are, since that block
   is pre-existing, unmodified ns-3 code.
3. Worth adding a companion CSV column / trace (e.g. counting frames sent
   per Stage-2 win) if you want to directly verify in results that TXOPs
   are now carrying more than one frame -- happy to add that if useful.
4. Re-derive whether PEdcaStage2Window (97 us in your sweep) is still an
   appropriate value once Stage-2 wins can now cover multi-frame TXOPs --
   the window governs how long OTHER eligible STAs can still join Stage 2
   to compete for the *next* win, not the winner's own TXOP duration, so
   it likely does not need to change for this fix alone, but worth
   confirming against your target draft's intent.
